<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-IAMA says Primac bid unconditional.</title>
<headline>RTRS-IAMA says Primac bid unconditional.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rural services group IAMA Ltd said on Thursday it had declared its offer for Primac Holdings Ltd unconditional.</p>
<p>IAMA is offering nine of its shares for every 10 Primac shares. Primac has rejected the IAMA offer.</p>
<p>IAMA said it had received acceptances for 16.2 percent of Primac shares with the offer set to close on February 28. Elders Australia Ltd owns about 17 percent of Primac.</p>
<p>At 3.20 p.m. (0420 GMT), IAMA shares were one cent up at A$2.85, while Primac shares were steady at A$3.00.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
